3667               /**********************************************************************
3668               
3669               /       EXPLANATION OF PAL8'S BUFFER ALLOCATION ALGORITHM
3670               
3671               /PASS1:
3672               
3673               /       THE INPUT BUFFER STARTS AT 5600 AND ENDS AT 7200
3674               /       THE INPUT HANDLER GOES IN 7200-7600.
3675               /       THERE IS NO OUTPUT HANDLER.
3676               /       HOWEVER, IF THE CURRENT INPUT HANDLER DOES NOT
3677               /       LOAD INTO 7200, THEN THE BUFFER SIZE IS INCREASED
3678               /       SO THAT THE INPUT BUFFER IS 5600-7600
3679               
3680               /PASS2 AND PASS3:
3681               
3682               /       THE OUTPUT BUFFER IS ALWAYS 1 BLOCK LONG, LOCATED
3683               /       AT 5600-6200.
3684               /       THE OUTPUT HANDLER RESIDES IN 6200-6600.
3685               /       THE INPUT HANDLER RESIDES IN 7200-7600.
3686               /       THE INPUT BUFFER NORMALLY RESIDES IN 6600-7200
3687               /       BUT MAY GROW OVER EITHER THE INPUT HANDLER AREA OR
3688               /       THE OUTPUT HANDLER AREA, IF EITHER OR BOTH OF THESE
3689               /       DON'T EXIST.
3690               
3691               /WHENEVER A BUFFER GROWS OVER A HANDLER AREA, THE MONITOR
3692               /HANDLER RESIDENCY TABLE IS SEARCHED TO SEE IF THERE
3693               /WERE ANY HANDLERS THERE.  IF ANY HANDLERS WERE THERE IN THE PAST,
3694               /THEY ARE NOW MARKED AS BEING NON-RESIDENT.
